221 1 1 1 true 2 | 1 2 2 | 1 | `Owned` row 0 is written by two owners — each row has one: key it by what distinguishes its writers | `Loose` is read while its owner `looping` has a run open — the rows a run writes are read once it closes | a `@query` wrote a row with no owner — a query answers, it writes no rows of its own; open a named owner's run around the write (`db.opened_run(db.owner_named(…))`)
